> dat1, fixed = list(ic50 + gam
> ~as.factor(drug),uk~1),random = uk ~ 1, data = dat1)

To fit the model you want you will need to call nlme with a formula
for the model and supply your own starting estimates for the
fixed-effects parameters.  The advantage of using an nlsList object as
the first argument is that starting estimates for a default version of
the fixed-effects parameters can be extracted from the nlsList
object.  Because you are using a non-default fixed specification
(which is probably a good idea) you will need to specify starting
estimates in the call.

