Your F1 and F3 were globals, with F2 being local to F1.  With that 
construction, F2 is defined during the execution of F1 and ceases to 
exist upon exit from F1.  If you want to define a function within F1 and 
have it persist, have you considered "assign"?

hope this helps.  spencer graves

