What about using

vec <- 1:10
vec2 <- c(vec[2:10],NA)

res <- vec + vec2

The additional NA is only put in to prevent an erroneous value when adding 
two differently sized vectors.

That should be pretty fast since no explicit looping takes place. There is 
only one explicit indexing involved and that only during the construction 
of vec2.

I use this kind of construction for a function where I calculate the 
running mean of a time series. It's pretty fast and avoids the memory 
intensive use of a temporary matrix.

HTH,
Gernot

