Jones, and Henrik Aalborg for their very useful help.

Second for the benefit of all I?ll try to summary what I have learned.  
Please fell free to correct if there any error in my interpretation.

The second problems were I multiply two big integers and I obtained NA as 
result.

This happen due to a change in the S-Plus design that produce what is know 
as integer overflow.  It is sufficient to add a decimal to just one of the 
numbers, and the others will be coerced from integer to double.

For more specific information refer to:
http://www.insightful.com/insightful_faq/dsp_article.asp?articleID=112

The first problem is more complicated but I?ll tell what I did to solve it.

I found that I have masked function.
When I used the command

masked()

I received the following:
?Random.seed?;   ?air?

Following I used

(rm(.Random.seed))
(rm( ?air?))

masked()
?air?

After this I supposed that a database called air was the problem I deleted 
it because it did not had relevance for me.  This ?air? is not the same as 
the s-plus example. So there were two databases with the same name.

After deleted the database the same error message appear so I decided to 
uninstall and install s-plus again saving to a file all important script, 
databases and results from analysis to a file in my document.

The problem did not appear after the new installation and I was able to 
import the database from spss and so far I have not received the error 
message in analysis.

The question that remains is; beside re-install s-plus what I was suppose to 
do with ?air? and the problem?

Thanks again, and is wonderful to have this user group list.

Sincerely,
José A. Bartolomei

