It's expected from the S scope rules.  I think it is `a little bit
strange' that you think it should work.

Recommended reading on the scope rules : `S Programming', Venables & 
Ripley (2000).

Hints:  sapply will be easier to use that unlist(lapply()), and s/lapply 
take a ... argument to pass S objects through,  Functions return their 
last value, so you don't need to assign, nor do you need an explicit call 
to return().

