	  The scoping rules are different in S-Plus and R.  I want code that 
will work in both.  Therefore, I push myself to explicitly pass all 
arguments by name in the function definition and in the "..." argument 
of calling functions like "lapply".  When I do this, I don't have to 
worry about whether I'm using S-Plus or R, and scripts I write using one 
are more likely to work without change in the other.

hope this helps.  spencer graves

