You have given us too few details of what you did to be sure, but one idea
is that P and d (or D?) are factors whose levels are not ordered as you
expected.  That's more or less confirmed by the tapply's you quote which
suggest that p (not P!) is a factor with levels "1" and "0" *in that
order*, so a logistic regression (done by the naive use of glm) of p on s
b and d would be of the log odds of "0" vs "1".

It's entirely possible that d also does not have the levels you think it 
has.

If that is not the explanation, please show us all the code you used
and summary() on your data frame.

