Dear Mark,

At 06:06 PM 9/13/2003 -0400, Leeds, Mark wrote:
> I have the following problem that
> I have spent a lot of time on but I
> can't figure out.
>
> I have a string called tickerstring
> that might be
>
> "ANL LN32"
>
>
>
> and i want to get rid of the digit piece.
> so that i get "ANL LN"
>
> i can't just take off the last two characters
> because the string could also be
>
> "ANL LN3" for example.
> I don't know how many digits will
> be on the end.
>
> thanks to anyone who could explain
> how to do this ?  I imagine that
> it can be done ?

Something like the following should do what you want:

> string <- "ANL LN32"
> substring(string, 1, regexpr("[0-9]*$", string) - 1)
[1] "ANL LN"

I hope that this helps,
 John
