Dear Hendry,

I assume that the "correlation" matrix (say, R)  that you want to use is 
actually positive-definite, and that you don't require that the 
correlations for your sample be exactly equal to the target values, but 
only equal in expectation. If so, then you can use the Cholesky square root 
of R. Using rnorm(), generate a matrix, say Z, of independent 
standard-normal variables of the required dimension. Then compute Z %*% 
chol(R).

I hope that this helps,
 John

